00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:05.349 align:start position:0%
the prehistoric stone circle came into  view when a dam in the spanish province  of casarus dropped to a quarter of its  usual capacity the stones were first  discovered in 1926  and have only been fully visible four  times since  the discovery is an unexpected side  effect of the worst drought in europe in  decades  in serbia the river danube is at its  lowest level in nearly a century  revealing the wreckages of 20 german  warships which were sunk during world  war ii  this is what remains from the war  between the army of the soviet union and  the german war flotilla there's about 10  000 kilograms of explosive devices here  we're not sure if they can explode but  you can imagine the problems if they do  in germany the drought has exposed  so-called hunger stones at sections of  the river rhine  centuries ago they were placed on dry  riverbeds to warn future generations  their exposure could signal famine  away from europe and a drought in china  has revealed ancient statues of buddha  on an island that's usually submerged  the statues are believed to be 600 years  old  i read in the newspaper the statues are  from the ming and king dynasties it's  rare to see weather like this i'm  worried i think it's a warning to us  rainfall in the yangtze basin has been  around 45 lower since july authorities  say as many as 66 rivers across  southwest china have dried up this  summer  with many scientists saying hotter days  as a result of global warming are here  to stay  more relics from the past are sure to  emerge victoria gatenbee al jazeera
 

